  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Discussion on the Paper by Andrieu, Doucet and Holenstein",
      "bbox": [
        170.1251983642578,
        39.52751922607422,
        407.9410095214844,
        47.82143783569336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "317",
      "bbox": [
        428.84710693359375,
        39.52751922607422,
        443.8030700683594,
        47.82143783569336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "latter situation is very speciﬁc, although it satisﬁes assumptions 1–4 that were made in the paper. In this",
      "bbox": [
        48.089813232421875,
        57.378700256347656,
        443.6120910644531,
        65.6905517578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "example, any method based on direct importance sampling, including the PIMH algorithm using an SMC",
      "bbox": [
        48.089813232421875,
        67.3412857055664,
        443.6093444824219,
        75.65313720703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "algorithm without resampling (i.e. sequential importance sampling), is bound to fail for all feasible values",
      "bbox": [
        48.089813232421875,
        77.30387115478516,
        443.6032409667969,
        85.61572265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of N when T is larger than, say, 17 (see the caption of Fig. 12). In contrast, Fig. 12 shows that the PIMH",
      "bbox": [
        48.089813232421875,
        87.2664566040039,
        443.61199951171875,
        95.57830810546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "algorithm using an embedded SMC algorithm with resampling at each step (as described in Section 2.2.1)",
      "bbox": [
        48.08802032470703,
        97.22904205322266,
        443.6084899902344,
        105.5408935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "can cope with dimensions as large as T =103. In addition, Fig. 12 also suggests that increasing N as O.T/",
      "bbox": [
        48.08802032470703,
        106.07691192626953,
        443.60076904296875,
        115.50372314453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is sufﬁcient to stabilize the acceptance rate. I would be happy to hear the authors’ comments on whether",
      "bbox": [
        48.0892333984375,
        117.15445709228516,
        443.61224365234375,
        125.46630859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the behaviour of PIMH sampling in this simple scenario can be inferred from known results about SMC",
      "bbox": [
        48.0892333984375,
        127.1170425415039,
        443.61065673828125,
        135.42889404296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "methods regarding the rate of convergence of ˆZN=Z as N increases.",
      "bbox": [
        48.0892333984375,
        135.34910583496094,
        302.306640625,
        145.3914794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "J. Cornebise (Statistical and Applied Mathematical Sciences Institute, Durham) and G. W. Peters",
      "bbox": [
        48.08952331542969,
        155.01243591308594,
        408.9100646972656,
        163.32427978515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(University of New South Wales, Sydney)",
      "bbox": [
        48.08953857421875,
        164.9750213623047,
        201.75302124023438,
        173.286865234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our comments on adaptive sequential Monte Carlo (SMC) methods relate to particle Metropolis–Hastings",
      "bbox": [
        48.08953857421875,
        174.93760681152344,
        443.6054992675781,
        183.24945068359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(PMH) sampling, which has acceptance probability given in equation (13) of the paper for proposed state",
